HippoLM Marlin FP4 vendored sources
====================================

This directory contains source code vendored from vLLM
(https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm), which is licensed under the
Apache License, Version 2.0. The full Apache 2.0 license text is in
LICENSE-APACHE-2.0 alongside this NOTICE.

Source of truth
---------------
The vendored sources are extracted from vLLM's stable-ABI Marlin FP4
path, snapshot circa vLLM 0.7/0.8. The vendored files are:

Hand-extracted wrappers (5 files, ~960 lines):
  marlin_kernel_only.cu
  marlin_repack_adapter.cu
  marlin_helpers.cu
  marlin_mm_only.cu
  marlin/gptq_marlin_repack_kernel_only.cu

Patched vLLM headers (~6,600 lines):
  marlin/kernel.h
  marlin/marlin.cuh          (patch: <iostream> dropped)
  marlin/marlin_dtypes.cuh
  marlin/marlin_mma.h
  marlin/marlin_template.h   (patch: #pragma once added)
  marlin/dequant.h
  marlin/kernel_selector.h
  core/scalar_type.hpp

Per-SM explicit-instantiation files (~290 lines, NVFP4 + FP8 × BF16/FP16):
  marlin/sm80_kernel_bfloat16_fe2m1f_bfloat16.cu
  marlin/sm80_kernel_bfloat16_fe4m3fn_bfloat16.cu
  marlin/sm80_kernel_float16_fe2m1f_float16.cu
  marlin/sm80_kernel_float16_fe4m3fn_float16.cu
  marlin/sm89_kernel_fe4m3fn_fe2m1f_bfloat16.cu

Helper:
  libtorch_stable/torch_utils.h

Modifications made for the vendored copy
----------------------------------------
The following changes were applied to the vLLM originals. They are
necessary for the standalone build to compile against torch 2.12 +
CUDA 13.0; none change the kernel semantics.

1. marlin/marlin.cuh — dropped ``#include <iostream>``. vLLM includes
   ``<iostream>`` at the top of the file, which transitively pulls in
   ``<bits/stringfwd.h>``. When processed inside ``namespace marlin``
   (as our standalone wrapper does), the standard library's allocator
   lookup fails with ``error: 'allocator' is not a template``.

2. marlin/marlin_template.h — added ``#pragma once`` at the top.
   vLLM relies on include-order idempotency in ``marlin.cu``. Our
   standalone build textually includes ``sm89_kernel_*.cu`` after
   ``marlin_template.h``; without the guard, template definitions
   (``marlin::scale_float`` etc.) are duplicated and nvcc errors.

3. libtorch_stable/torch_utils.h — replaced vLLM's torch 2.9.1 shim
   (which used ``torch_get_current_cuda_blas_handle``) with a 36-line
   version that defines ``STD_TORCH_CHECK_NOT_IMPLEMENTED`` via
   ``<torch/headeronly/util/Exception.h>`` and provides the raw CUDA
   helpers via ``<torch/csrc/stable/...>``. The full vLLM shim depends
   on torch 2.12's stable ABI symbols (``Tensor::const_data_ptr``,
   ``Tensor::mutable_data_ptr``, ``TORCH_BOX``) which torch 2.12.0+cu130
   does provide, but we vendor only the minimal subset.

4. C++ namespace wrap — every ``namespace vllm { ... }`` declaration
   in the vendored headers is wrapped as
   ``namespace marlin { namespace vllm { ... } }``. References to
   ``vllm::ScalarType``, ``vllm::kFloat16``, etc. are rewritten to
   ``marlin::vllm::ScalarType`` / ``marlin::vllm::kFloat16`` throughout.
   This avoids leaking any global ``vllm::`` symbol from the
   standalone .so while keeping the mechanical edits minimal
   (no semantic rename). The mangled C++ symbol for
   ``marlin::marlin_mm`` therefore becomes
   ``_ZN6marlin9marlin_mmE...RKN6marlin4vllm10ScalarTypeE...``
   (cf. vLLM's original ``_ZN4vllm10ScalarTypeE``).

5. STABLE_TORCH_LIBRARY_IMPL removed — the standalone wrappers
   ``marlin_kernel_only.cu`` and ``marlin_repack_adapter.cu`` do not
   register the kernels via ``STABLE_TORCH_LIBRARY_IMPL``; they
   expose ``extern "C"`` entries for ctypes. This decouples us from
   the ``torch::stable::Tensor`` ABI and lets us load the .so against
   any torch 2.12.x+cu130 build.

Build environment
-----------------
Toolchain pinned as of 2026-07-08:
  - torch 2.12.0+cu130 (CPython 3.11)
  - CUDA 13.0 (nvcc 13.0.88 from cuda-toolkit-13-0)
  - driver 580.76.05+
  - gcc 11 host compiler
  - SM architectures in scope: sm80 (A100), sm89 (RTX 4090), sm120
    (5060 Ti / RTX 50 series). sm70 / sm75 / sm100 are out of scope.

